    <worksheet name='Insight 3 - What is Ireland doing with its Winfall?'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='1'>Insight 3 - What is Ireland doing with its &quot;Oil&quot;Money?
</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#b4b4b4' underline='true'>Gross</run>
            <run fontalignment='1'> vs </run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#59a14f' underline='true'>Net Debt</run>
            <run fontalignment='1'>, </run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#a0cbe8' underline='true'>Cash &amp; Bond assets</run>
            <run fontalignment='1'> and</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#f28e2b' underline='true'> FIF &amp; ICNF savings </run>
            <run fontalignment='1'>(€ bn): 2012 - 2030</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>Gross and Net irish government debt along with cash and bond assets. Furutre Ireland Fund(FIF) and Infrastructure, Climate and Nature Fund balances have forecasted amounts from IFAC until 2030. Partial overlap of Cash and Bond and FIF &amp; ICNF funds so separated out to prevent double counting and ensure proper separation.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
